  "body": "Follow-up from PR #2997 (#2987).\n\nPR #2997 judges the first traverse of a 3+2 operation against the machine table. For a head tilt past 90 degrees, the tool axis points down toward the table. A higher clearance plane then stands lower in the world. The verdict `FirstTraverseLow` can only say \"raise the clearance height\", which is the wrong repair there.\n\nSo PR #2997 gives such a plane a note (\"the machine table is not judged on this tilted plane: the tool axis points down toward the table\") and no verdict. The post is not blocked.\n\nRisk: the first rapid of such an operation can go into the table, and no law refuses it.\n\nWork:\n1. Add a verdict that says \"lower the clearance plane\" (or an equivalent repair) for a tool axis that points down. It touches `camcraft-sim`, the app, the UI and MCP.\n2. Block the post on it, as `FirstTraverseLow` does.\n3. Add pinning tests: a head tilt past 90 degrees that is refused, and one that is clear.\n",
